---
title: Spicy Roasted Butter Beans
servings: 2
course: Snack
locale: en
difficulty: Easy
---

Preheat oven to 160°C.

Drain and rinse the @butter beans, chickpeas, cannellini beans, or similar{1%tin}, then spread on a kitchen towel and gently pat them dry. Make sure they are completely dry so that they will crisp up in the oven.

Add the @olive oil{1%tbsp} to a bowl and mix in the spices (@salt{0.5%tsp}, @garlic powder{0.5%tsp}, @paprika{0.5%tsp}, @chilli powder{0.25%tsp}, and @black pepper{0.25%tsp}). Fold in the beans until evenly coated.

Transfer onto a baking sheet lined with baking paper and spread out evenly. Roast for 35 to ~{40%minutes} until crunchy.

> Best enjoyed as soon as they cool down. They can be stored for up to 24 hours in an air-tight container at room temperature.